      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62df7cd83e007e467295c4e1|full_name}\n\nThanks for the question.\n\nThe intention is not to exceed the maximum capacity set by the world creator.\n\nThe request is to allow authorized users (for example group moderators or event staff) to adjust the player capacity within the creator-defined maximum limit when creating an instance.\n\nFor example, if a world has a maximum capacity of 25, an authorized user could choose any value between 2–25 at instance creation.\n\nThe goal is simply to allow trusted staff members to configure the instance capacity when starting an event, without requiring the world creator to be present.\n\nChanging the capacity while the instance is already running is not required for this request. Instance creation control would already solve most use cases.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-03-11T01:34:17.345Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "We need a way to delegate \"World Capacity\" control to people other than the original creator.\n\n​The Problem:\n\nCurrently, only the creator can change the capacity. If the creator is offline during a large event, staff cannot adjust the player limit to manage lag or accommodate more guests.\n\n​Proposed Solution:\n\nAdd a permission setting in the Group or World dashboard that allows specific roles to change the Instance Capacity (Soft/Hard cap).\n\n​This is essential for professional event management and community-run worlds where the uploader isn't always the one managing the floor.",
